{
  "id": "COMPOUND:17358 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Negombatoperoxide B is implicated in the regulation of Phosphodiesterase 6C through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Negombatoperoxide B acts as a target for several molecular entities, including the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex and LAMA-84, which in turn target Ardisianoside C. These intermediaries ultimately lead to the activation of Phosphodiesterase 6C. The relationship between Negombatoperoxide B and Phosphodiesterase 6C is thus mediated through a series of molecular interactions, with the exact mechanism of action of Negombatoperoxide B remaining unclear. The evidence supports a hierarchical pathway where Negombatoperoxide B serves as a bridge to the enzyme, though the precise functional role of Negombatoperoxide B in this context remains to be elucidated.",
